-- ============================================================================
-- 34: render-replica LIVE — REAL HUD via the engine's own TA quads (HUDQ tail).
-- SUPERSEDES the procedural/reconstructed HUD lineage (finding:replica_live_hud*):
-- instead of re-drawing the bars/digits from GSTA fields, we now CAPTURE the engine's
-- ACTUAL HUD/composite TA quads from the surviving render pass and ship them as a new
-- HUDQ wire tail, so the client draws MVC2's real HUD pixel-perfect. feat/render-replica-live.
-- Pinned 2026-06-14.
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:hud_surviving_pass SET kind='code',
  ref='core/network/maplecast_mirror.cpp:1748-1782 (serverPublish) + core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp:571-659 (rend_start_render) + ta_ctx.cpp:67-73 (single-slot QueueRender)',
  note='MVC2 emits MULTIPLE STARTRENDER passes per video frame; flycast QueueRender is single-slot so all but one are tactx_Recycle dropped. On MVC2 the SURVIVING pass (the one that reaches DequeueRender->render()->serverPublish on headless) IS the HUD/composite pass (op~573 tr~42, isRTT=0, body flattened to a composite quad). rend_norend runs ta_parse on CPU and builds the FULL ctx->rend (Renderer_if.cpp:482-490), so the HUD polys are ALREADY parsed every frame on the surviving pass — collectHudQuads reads that parsed rc with ZERO extra ta_parse beyond the one mc_oracle_charPassCapture already does. The CHARACTER pass (per-part body quads, op~265 tr~2024) is the one QueueRender DROPS; CHARQ captures it upstream at rend_start_render. The two are distinct passes; the HUD lives in the surviving one.';

UPSERT source:hud_ta_qdiag_inventory SET kind='oracle',
  ref='MAPLECAST_QDIAG HUD dump (collectHudQuads -> /dev/shm/mc_hud_qdiag.log) + tools/validate_hud_ta.py on a live in-match prod TA stream (mc_engine_ta.bin, surviving HUD pass)',
  note='LIVE in-match prod HUD-pass poly inventory (the QDIAG enumeration that set MAX_HUD + the discriminator thresholds). The surviving pass carried 82 polys with >=3 verts; the discriminator (cy<120 || cy>=420) && w<320 && h<200 && fmt!=7 KEEPS 78 and DROPS 4 — the 4 dropped are the full-screen composite/backdrop (w 13003..14.5M px, the screen flatten/clear quads). y-distribution top(<120)=65 (life bars/meters/timer/portraits/names) bottom(>=420)=13 (tag-team standby bars). ALL HUD polys: textured, PVR para type 4 (Polygon, NOT type-5 Sprite), fmt=1 (font/glyph) or 2 (portrait), Offset=1, Col_Type 1/2/3 (INTENSITY float, base=0x3f800000=1.0) — so the per-team bar TINT comes from the FONT/glyph TEXTURE, not vertex modulate (the task spec assumption of ARGB8888 per-team modulate is INFERRED-wrong for these polys; col[] is captured verbatim and the client decodes via the shipped pcw Col_Type). Distinct bar TCWs: 0809be00 (FONT glyph atlas), 08080000 (flat bar fill), 0809de00/0809e000 (portrait/icon). MAX_HUD=256 = 3.3x the observed 78.';

UPSERT source:hud_textures_resident SET kind='reference',
  ref='source:hud_real_art_source (FONT.BIN/PLxx_FAC) + docs/RENDER-REPLICA-RECORDING-FORMAT.md (static 8MB VRAM prefix + palette tail)',
  note='The HUD textures the bars/digits sample (FONT.BIN font + portrait glyphs) are decoded into VRAM at match-LOAD, before any in-match STARTRENDER. So each HUD quad\'s tcw resolves against the already-shipped static 8MB VRAM prefix (+ the palette tail) — no extra texture wire is needed for the HUDQ tail; it ships only the per-frame screen geometry (corners/UV/color/control words).';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta SET
  statement='SUPERSEDES the procedural HUD (finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix and the whole replica_live_hud* reconstruction lineage): the render-replica LIVE client can now draw MVC2\'s ACTUAL HUD pixel-perfect from the engine\'s OWN TA quads, instead of re-deriving bars/digits from GSTA fields. SERVER (this commit, feat/render-replica-live): (1) collectHudQuads(rc) in core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp — sibling to collectScreenQuads, reuses the SAME dual min/max vertex walk (rc.idx-indexed for op/pt + non-autosort tr; rc.verts-direct for autosort tr). NO cy<=20 strip, NO textured-only gate. Discriminator KEEPS small/medium HUD polys ((cy<TOPY=120 || cy>=BOTY=420) && w<MAXW=320 && h<MAXH=200 && fmt!=7), DROPS the oversized full-screen composite/backdrop + fmt==7; all 4 thresholds env-overridable (MAPLECAST_HUD_TA_{TOPY,BOTY,MAXW,MAXH}) so a QDIAG re-run tunes WITHOUT a rebuild. Per poly emits 4 SUBMIT-ORDER corners x[4]/y[4] (HUD bars are angled parallelograms, NOT bbox), 4 UVs, 4 per-vertex base color words repacked to ARGB8888 ((A<<24)|(R<<16)|(G<<8)|B from flycast col[0..3]={R,G,B,A}), and pcw/isp/tsp/tcw verbatim, into static HudQuad s_hud[256]; published via mc_oracle_hudQuads(). (2) Collected in mc_oracle_charPassCapture BEFORE maplecast_replica_live::onRenderFrame, with its own read-only idempotent ta_parse(ctx,true), so the HUDQ tail and the frame body are the SAME video frame (the HUD pass is the surviving/last STARTRENDER pass; the replica capture is drop-old last-pass-wins, so they align). (3) HUDQ tail in core/network/maplecast_replica_live.cpp captureFrame — the THIRD variable tail, strictly AFTER the GFX tail + palette tail: u32 magic=0x48554451 (\'HUDQ\' LE) + u32 nHud + nHud x 96-byte HudQuad{ f32 x[4],y[4],u[4],v[4]; u32 col[4],pcw,isp,tsp,tcw }; total updated +8+nHud*96; present ONLY when MAPLECAST_HUD_TA armed AND nHud>0 (steady HUD-off path byte-identical, older clients skip via the magic). static_assert sizeof(HudQuad)==96. Gated MAPLECAST_HUD_TA (off by default) + in-match (0x8C289624); READ-ONLY (ta_parse builds ctx->rend, never writes guest), determinism-safe; prod hot path unaffected when unset. The 96-byte HudQuad is the wire interface the sprite-render-expert client consumes. CLIENT (parallel, sprite-render-expert) draws the HUDQ quads instead of renderHudPass(). docs/RENDER-REPLICA-RECORDING-FORMAT.md documents the FRMx tail order + the HudQuad layout.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_validated SET
  statement='VALIDATED quad-level (no GPU). The HUDQ tail IS derived from the same ta_parse the render path runs, so the acceptance test is a self-consistency proof: tools/validate_hud_ta.py re-runs the IDENTICAL discriminator over the engine\'s raw PVR TA stream (parse_engine_ta.walk, byte-exact flycast TaTypeLut) and emits the expected HUD inventory; --hudq cross-checks a captured live HUDQ tail byte-for-byte (count + x[4]/y[4] within 0.01px + tcw/tsp identical). On a live in-match prod TA stream it produced 78 expected HUD quads (TOPY=120 BOTY=420 MAXW=320 MAXH=200), matching the MAPLECAST_QDIAG mc_hud_qdiag.log KEEP count exactly. BUILD: headless (cmake MAPLECAST_HEADLESS=ON) compiled+linked clean on the dev box 65.109.77.178 (the static_assert sizeof(HudQuad)==96 is a compile gate, so the wire struct is provably 96B), stripped md5 48364cd8d128de2b620ed749c2cb0a8d, no GPU libs. STAGED to prod 149.28.44.118 /opt/maplecast/flycast-hudq-staged (md5-verified == dev build); the live service was NOT restarted (user-coordinated). RUN-LIVE step (user): set MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 (+ MAPLECAST_QDIAG=1 for the inventory log) in the headless env and swap the staged binary in; then scp /dev/shm/mc_hud_qdiag.log + a captured HUDQ tail and run validate_hud_ta.py --hudq for the final byte-for-byte PASS against a real running frame.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_open_multistrip SET
  statement='OPEN refinement (not blocking; logged honestly). collectHudQuads emits ONE HudQuad per PolyParam, taking the FIRST 4 submit-order verts as the quad corners. The QDIAG inventory shows most HUD bars ARE single 4-vert parallelograms (the life bars, meter bars, single boxed digits), but SOME polys are longer tri-strips (verts=8/14/16/32 — e.g. a multi-glyph text run / name plate submitted as one strip), where the first 4 verts capture only the FIRST quad of the strip and the remaining strip-quads are dropped. For pixel-perfect multi-glyph HUD text the collector should expand a tri-strip into (count-2) triangles -> (count/2-1) quads, emitting one HudQuad per strip-quad (with bbox/discriminator applied per strip, not per first-quad). Deferred: the bars/timer/combo (the high-value HUD) are single quads and already correct; the long-strip text runs (names) are tier-2. Confirm on the live MAPLECAST_QDIAG mc_hud_qdiag.log which kept polys have verts>4 and how many distinct screen-glyphs they cover before deciding the strip-expansion is worth the wire.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta->supersedes->finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_open_multistrip->cites->source:hud_ta_qdiag_inventory;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta->cites->source:hud_surviving_pass;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta->cites->source:hud_ta_qdiag_inventory;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta->cites->source:hud_textures_resident;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_validated->cites->source:hud_ta_qdiag_inventory;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_validated->cites->source:hud_surviving_pass;
